- **telegram**: an always-on Claude session answers my Telegram bot, on the Mac named in `__PROFILE_DIR__/telegram/ACTIVE_HOST` (working folder `__TELEGRAM_WORKDIR__`, screen session `claude-tg`). I often drive sessions from my phone, so keep replies short and readable on a small screen. The Telegram plugin is off in settings.json on purpose; only that session turns it on (`~/.claude/telegram-settings.json`). Never start a second copy or run `claude mcp list` inside it: a second poller steals messages. Status: `__HARNESS_DIR__/modules/telegram/install.sh --status`.
  - To merge a PR when I ask from Telegram ("merge job-hunt 3"), run `__HARNESS_DIR__/scripts/pr-merge.sh <repo> <number>`. It refuses drafts, conflicts, red or running checks and stacked PRs, then squash-merges. Reply with its one-line result.
